{"title":"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram, the rectangular solid and the cube have equal volumes.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>The length of each edge of the cube is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9ecdebcf4d4b2b0675e9fb39272bb63cbd0dcb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 4 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 8 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 15 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can use the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Volume\" title=\"Volume\">volume</a> of a rectangular prism to find the side length of the cube. \n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the volume of the rectangular solid that we know the side length of. We can then set up an equation involving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/d/12d58aa29201da09d8e620f8698e3a37547f6b4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8be0b8b376c3480092cea50ca1d7e794d4effc7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V = 2 \\times 4 \\times 8 = 8 \\times 8 = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"220\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> be the length of each edge of the cube. \n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Since a cube is a special rectangular prism, where all of the lengths are equal to each other, its volume must be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/023a8d1ea77121d397018d0950691b5b8981e194.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"17\" />. This means:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a3158e6c9e5b21ecb604f3ecfb77869067538e5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l^3 = V = 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/95859998f834e32439f61ccbe13b837705a2e5f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l = \\sqrt[3]{64}  = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal\">2006 CEMC Pascal</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems (page does not exist)\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_CEMC_Pascal_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2006 CEMC Pascal Probl